{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And every animal that splits the hoof.</b> Even though He omitted the names, since the rest of the animals are known by their names, He gives you a sign among them to distinguish the clean from the unclean. <b>Splits the hoof and is fully cloven into two hooves, brings up the cud.</b> There are three signs: if it has no hoof, such as a dog or cat — forbidden; and if it is cloven but does not bring up the cud, such as a pig — forbidden; and even if it has a hoof, since it is not cloven, such as a horse and donkey — forbidden; and if it brings up the cud and has no hoof, such as a camel, hare, and rock badger — forbidden."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:43.614046077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}